+# TASK-064 round 1 report
+
+Counts below belong to commit `203023c781d0ec682d93a177488188a59f0cda86`. At step 12 the working tree held uncommitted changes; `git status --short` is quoted there. This report file was completed after that snapshot.
+
+## Files changed
+
+- `bridge/cursor-bridge/bridge_env.py`
+- `bridge/cursor-bridge/review-guard.py`
+- `bridge/cursor-bridge/conformance-check.py`
+- `bridge/cursor-bridge/MANIFEST.json` (regenerated by `python tools/make-manifest.py`; not edited by hand)
+- `tests/test_conformance_check.py` (cases appended; no existing case edited)
+- `tests/test_review_guard.py` (one case appended; no existing case edited)
+- `tests/test_release_s_records_gate.py` (one case appended; no existing case edited)
+- `docs/BUILDER_NOTES.md` (one dated line)
+- `handoff/TASK-064-r1-report.md`
+
+`bridge/cursor-bridge/VERSION` was restored with `git restore` after the manifest run and is not listed by `git status --short`. `tests/test_program_branch_rule.py` and `tests/fixtures/github/` were not edited. No existing assertion in the three test files was rewritten for the auto-merge line or the `deleted` word: the new lines are covered by the supervisor's cases and by the cases appended here.
+
+## Summary
+
+`bridge_env.py` now has the one GitHub reader: `branch_rule`, `repo_settings`, `pull_refs`, `head_state`, `latest_of_each` and `ci_class`, each GitHub call a single windowless GET through `GH_COMMAND + ["api", path]` with a 30-second limit and no retry, returning value, none, or cannot read. `conformance-check.py` asks `branch_rule` for the default branch and prints a NOTE when that rule cannot be read. `premerge` and `premerge-records` print the repository's auto-merge setting after a successful verdict, and the closing `GATE-INTEGRITY` line of `verify` and of `premerge` says `deleted` or `rewritten` as the snapshot was.
+
+## R1-R14
+
+1. R1. `_gh_get` (`bridge_env.py` 3887-3919) runs `list(GH_COMMAND) + ["api", path]` at call time, `GH_COMMAND` and `GH_API_TIMEOUT` at 3838-3839, with `stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL`, `creationflags=NO_WINDOW`, UTF-8 replacement, and one call; a missing `gh`, a time-out, a non-zero exit, or a body that is not the expected JSON is cannot read.
+2. R2. `ANSWER_VALUE`, `ANSWER_NONE` and `ANSWER_CANNOT` are at 3840-3842; `_answer` (3875-3884) puts `answer`, `reason` and `source` on every reader result, with a non-empty reason wherever the answer is cannot read.
+3. R3. `branch_rule` (4006-4041) percent-encodes the branch with `urllib.parse.quote(branch, safe="")`, unions `_protection_contexts` (3936-3969) and `_rules_contexts` (3972-4003), and treats only `_unprotected` (3922-3924) plus a rules success, or two successes that name no check, as none; any other failure is cannot read with `source` `protection` or `rules` and `contexts` `[]`.
+4. R4. `repo_settings` (4044-4057) reads `repos/<repo>` and returns `allow_auto_merge` and `default_branch`, or cannot read when the reply is not a success or `allow_auto_merge` is not a boolean; `repo_settings(repo)` takes no folder, and `cwd` is optional.
+5. R5. `pull_refs` (4060-4075) reads `repos/<repo>/pulls/<number>` and returns `base` and `head`, or cannot read.
+6. R6. `head_state` (4131-4147) asks check runs (`filter=all`), commit statuses and workflow runs through `_read_list` (4096-4128), which sends `page` and `per_page` until `total_count` is reached and stops by page 100; a failed page, a page that adds no entry, or a `total_count` that is not a non-negative integer makes that list the `source` of cannot read.
+7. R7. `latest_of_each` (4219-4281) keeps the latest run by `workflow_id` and `event`, then `run_number` and `run_attempt`; checks of a latest run by name, and checks no run made by name and app id, through `_last_by` (4175-4193); statuses by `context` and `updated_at`. Each kept entry is the dict it was given.
+8. R8. `ci_class` (4284-4305) returns `passed`, `pending`, `skipped` or `failed` from the closed lists; an unknown conclusion or state is `failed`.
+9. R9. `conformance-check.py` 919-937 calls `bridge_env.branch_rule(nwo, branch, cwd=ws)` after the existing `gh repo view` read: value prints the OK row with at most four context names, none prints the MISSING row `branch protection exists but requires no status check; N6 needs the gate job required`, cannot read prints the NOTE beginning `cannot read the branch rule (`, and a loaded module with no `branch_rule` prints `the branch rule was not read`. The `--offline`, `cannot verify through gh` and `cannot read gh's answer` notes are unchanged.
+10. R10. `cmd_premerge` 1259-1270 and `cmd_premerge_records` 1525-1536 call `bridge_env.repo_settings("{owner}/{repo}", cwd=cwd)` after the merge line and print one of the three auto-merge lines; the verdict, the exit and the record are unchanged, and the lines contain no `--auto`.
+11. R11. `snapshot_rewritten` returns `"deleted"` at line 332 when the file is gone and `"rewritten"` at line 335 when the hash differs; `cmd_verify` line 993 and `cmd_premerge` line 1193 put that word into the closing line. The indented lines, the `"missing"` return and the `None` return are unchanged, and both commands still call `record_flagged_launch` or return 1 as before.
+12. R12. `test_r083_the_required_check_row_follows_the_branch_rule` in `tests/test_conformance_check.py` drives value, none and cannot read through the supervisor's stand-in and the recorded replies, and the cannot-read row is a NOTE whose detail starts `cannot read the branch rule (` and contains `review-guard.py ready answers CANNOT CHECK`. `test_r083_a_bridge_env_without_branch_rule_does_not_invent_a_row` covers the missing attribute.
+13. R13. `test_r084_a_premerge_that_is_not_a_success_prints_no_auto_merge_line` in `tests/test_review_guard.py` and `test_r084_premerge_records_without_a_pull_request_prints_no_auto_merge_line` in `tests/test_release_s_records_gate.py` use the stand-in and a recorded reply, in process, with `GH_COMMAND` replaced.
+14. R14. Each added case names `R-083` or `R-084` and the D-002 element `conformance_check` or `review_guard`. The parametrized conformance case has `ids=["value", "none", "cannot-read"]`.
+
+## Mutations
+
+None were applied by hand. No mutation script is in the diff.
